      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: Can you maybe reconsider adding Protonmail for signup? It seems like this decision was made a few years ago when Protonmail wasn't as big as it is now. Protonmail has taken many security measures to prevent it from being used for malicious intent or spam.\nPeople also use it for their complete toolchain, as they now have a drive to store files, a VPN service, and a calendar service. Users who prefer email services that prioritize privacy should not be treated unfairly, which is the case here, even if it is not intended.\nAny email service, and especially self-hosted email, is much more vulnerable to malicious attacks on your services, and yet you allow their use, but not something like Protonmail.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
